1
00:00:00,444 --> 00:00:05,005
This is Tacit. Sealed bid auctions
and shielded escrow on Zcash.

2
00:00:05,055 --> 00:00:06,361
The price is public.

3
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:07,466
The bidders are not.

4
00:00:10,213 --> 00:00:12,474
Every auction on a public chain leaks.

5
00:00:12,524 --> 00:00:15,221
Bids get sniped and buyers get tracked.

6
00:00:15,271 --> 00:00:20,622
And Zcash has no smart contracts, so fair
markets needed a middleman you had to trust.

7
00:00:20,672 --> 00:00:22,093
Tacit fixes both.

8
00:00:23,794 --> 00:00:26,834
Tacit runs in your browser,
on mainnet and testnet,

9
00:00:26,884 --> 00:00:30,875
built on drand timelock encryption and
two of three FROST vaults on Ironwood.

10
00:00:32,553 --> 00:00:35,639
Make a wallet with a recovery
phrase and a passcode.

11
00:00:35,689 --> 00:00:40,588
It syncs by decrypting blocks locally, so the
server never learns which coins are yours.

12
00:00:42,671 --> 00:00:46,371
A seller sets a reserve, a
bond and a bidding window.

13
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:50,262
Their browser, an operator and
an arbiter create a fresh vault,

14
00:00:50,312 --> 00:00:54,633
one key share each, and Tacit shows
exactly who could move the money.

15
00:00:56,324 --> 00:01:01,204
Every bidder deposits the same bond, so
the chain shows nothing about amounts.

16
00:01:01,254 --> 00:01:03,798
The bid is encrypted to
a future drand round,

17
00:01:03,848 --> 00:01:06,530
so nobody can open it early, not even us.

18
00:01:08,224 --> 00:01:11,665
When the round is published,
every bid opens at once.

19
00:01:11,715 --> 00:01:15,710
The agents recompute the winner
and cosign one shielded payout,

20
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:17,832
and your browser audits every step.

21
00:01:17,882 --> 00:01:19,055
Settled honestly.

22
00:01:20,754 --> 00:01:23,546
The proof page audits
every auction in public.

23
00:01:23,596 --> 00:01:27,155
And our first auction with real
ZEC has settled on mainnet,

24
00:01:27,205 --> 00:01:28,826
and passed the same audit.

25
00:01:30,513 --> 00:01:32,385
The same vaults power escrow.

26
00:01:32,435 --> 00:01:35,628
The buyer pays in and releases
when the deal is done,

27
00:01:35,678 --> 00:01:38,442
and nobody on chain can
tell it was an escrow.

28
00:01:41,434 --> 00:01:42,953
Anyone can be an arbiter.

29
00:01:43,003 --> 00:01:45,123
One binary, two commands.

30
00:01:45,173 --> 00:01:48,822
The more independent agents,
the stronger every market gets.

31
00:01:50,534 --> 00:01:52,949
Tacit. Sealed markets on Zcash.

32
00:01:52,999 --> 00:01:54,682
Open source, live today.

33
00:01:54,732 --> 00:01:55,858
Audit it yourself.
